  "339": {
    "inputs": {
      "value": "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> (S1) is Yennie, a young woman with a digital-host look: her facial features, hairstyle and youthful age appearance come from <Picture 1>, and her outfit from <Picture 2>. She is the first speaker, sitting on the left half of the sofa.\n<Subject 2> (S2) is Linsey, a young woman: her facial features, hairstyle and youthful age appearance come from <Picture 4>, and her outfit from <Picture 3>. She is the second speaker, sitting on the right half of the sofa.\n<Picture 5> is the living-room scene reference providing the environment, spatial layout, the sofa, and the environment lighting for all shots.\n<Audio 1> is the voice-timbre reference for <Subject 1> (S1). Only the vocal timbre, texture, speaking quality, and delivery character are referenced; the original signal, wording, phonemes, breaths, pauses, timing, and background sounds are not copied.\n\nsummary:\nreference generation - Two digital-host friends sit side by side on a sofa in a living room at night and chat in shot/reverse-shot about H3's facial expression acting, each demonstrating a different expression live to test it, ending with laughter.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Picture 1> (Yennie's facial features, in [Shot 1] and [Shot 3]): fully_preserved - face, hairstyle, age and expression base stay identical to the reference across shots.\n<Picture 2> (Yennie's outfit, in [Shot 1] and [Shot 3]): fully_preserved - her clothing stays exactly as in the reference, never changes.\n<Picture 3> (Linsey's outfit, in [Shot 1] and [Shot 2]): fully_preserved - her clothing stays exactly as in the reference, never changes.\n<Picture 4> (Linsey's facial features, in [Shot 1] and [Shot 2]): fully_preserved - face, hairstyle, age and expression base stay identical to the reference.\n<Picture 5> (living room at night, all shots): fully_preserved - the environment, spatial layout, the sofa and its evening lighting are preserved as-is from the reference in every shot.\n<Audio 1> (voice reference for <Subject 1> (S1) in [Shot 1] and [Shot 3]): reference - only the vocal timbre, texture, speaking quality, and delivery character are referenced. The original signal, wording, phonemes, breaths, pauses, timing, and background sounds are not copied.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe entire video contains no visible text of any kind, including subtitles, captions, titles, logos, watermarks, brand marks, signs, interface text, symbols, icons, stickers, or text-like graphics. No subtitles are rendered at any opacity; subtitle visibility is zero.\nHandheld camera with gentle natural sway and slow breathing drift throughout.\n\n[Shot 1] Medium two-shot: <Subject 1> (S1) Yennie and <Subject 2> (S2) Linsey sit side by side on the sofa, turned slightly toward each other, their faces and outfits matching their reference pictures; both blink naturally. Yennie turns her head toward Linsey to catch her attention, then says in a confident, show-off tone, <d>[Chinese] H3 表情演技真的强，你看，我先来个得意的。</d> while saying it she raises one eyebrow, curls the corner of her mouth into a smug smile and lifts her chin, holding the proud expression for half a second so Linsey can see it, then relaxes with a small wink. A soft fabric rustle accompanies her turn.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:05.000, over-the-shoulder single close-up of <Subject 2> (S2) Linsey from Yennie's side: Linsey first tilts her head and studies Yennie's expression appraisingly, gives a small nod, then says in a measured, slightly amused tone, <d>[Chinese] 嗯，像那么回事。那我来个高冷的，准备好了。</d> as she speaks she lets her face go flat and cool — eyes dropping downcast, chin lifted, lips pressed into a calm line — holding the aloof look for about a second before raising one eyebrow as if waiting for judgment. Yennie's shoulder stays in the left frame edge. She blinks naturally. Hard cut.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:10.000, single close-up of <Subject 1> (S1) Yennie with Linsey's shoulder at the right frame edge: the moment Yennie sees Linsey's aloof face she breaks into a \"噗\" laugh, her shoulders shaking lightly, then points at Linsey and says in a teasing, laughing tone, <d>[Chinese] 噗哈哈哈，你这也太端了，还是我自然。</d> she ends by doing a relaxed natural expression — a quick blink and an easy grin — and the two exchange a laughing glance as the shot holds for a moment of afterglow. Both blink naturally. Hard cut at the end.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nSoft room ambience at night: low air-conditioning hum and faint distant city sound, light fabric rustles as the two shift and turn on the sofa, gentle room reverb on voices. Non-verbal reactions: Yennie's burst of laughter with light shoulder-shaking in Shot 3, soft amused breaths between lines. Levels stay natural and intimate, matching the handheld breathing feel.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A"
    },
